  "policy": "BLENT_RUNTIME_HASH_CACHE_ENTRIES defaults to 64, accepts 0..256; zero clears retained entries at the next admitted lookup and disables memoization. Invalid/non-Unicode values reject cache-key admission. Version execution, manifest validation and platform/config reads remain fresh.",
  "ownership": "One process-lifetime Mutex<Memo> owns at most 256 canonical PathBuf/stat/digest entries. There are no retained file handles, contents, frames, callbacks or native leases. Each admitted hash call owns its original File and 64 KiB buffer; its miss reads at most 512 MiB+1 byte and verifies descriptor metadata before insertion. The mutex never spans content reads or native process execution. Hits copy a 32-byte digest; no borrowed entry escapes. Eviction and disable drop entries, process exit ends the static owner, and poisoned/invalid admission retains only the bounded existing value state. Native descriptor counts are unchanged after creating, hashing and unlinking more files than the active retention limit.",
  "identity": "Keys include canonical path, device, inode, size, mode, nanosecond mtime and ctime. Requires coherent filesystem metadata; this advisory optimization is not authentication or native-ownership evidence. Same-size rewrites with restored mtime, replacement, symlink retargeting, absent files, every metadata field and every capacity 0..256 are permanently tested. Omitting ctime deliberately fails the real same-size/restored-mtime regression; correct source is restored and the final suite passes.",
